/// MISCOMPILE (v-compiler-ml stress probe, 2026-07-16) — a SELF-RECURSIVE call on the payload binders of
/// a TUPLE-OF-TWO-SUMS match reads WRONG values. `cdz check` CLEAN (exit 0); `cdz compile` SUCCEEDS; RUNS
/// WRONG. This is the HM UNIFICATION dispatch shape — `match (a, b) with (TArrow(a1,a2), TArrow(b1,b2)) =>
/// unify(a2, b2)` — so a self-hosted type-checker's core silently misunifies.
///
///   def unify(a: Ty, b: Ty) = match (a, b) with
///     | (TInt, TInt) => 1
///     | (TBool, TBool) => 1
///     | (TArrow(a1,a2), TArrow(b1,b2)) => unify(a2, b2)
///     | (_, _) => 0
///   unify(TArrow(TInt,TBool), TArrow(TInt,TInt))
///     — the arrow arm recurses unify(a2,b2) = unify(TBool, TInt), which MUST be 0 (TBool ≠ TInt).
///     RETURNS 1.  (want 0)
///
/// SHARP DISCRIMINATORS (all verified 2026-07-16, each isolates the trigger):
///   • The payload binders bind CORRECTLY: matching the same `(a,b)` tuple-of-arrows and returning
///     tag(a1)*1000+tag(a2)*100+tag(b1)*10+tag(b2) gives the right 110 — so destructuring is fine; it is
///     the SELF-RECURSIVE CALL passing a2/b2 that reads wrong.
///   • SEPARATE (non-recursive) helper: `(TArrow(a1,a2), TArrow(b1,b2)) => eq2(a2, b2)` → CORRECT (0).
///   • INLINE nested match: `(TArrow(a1,a2), TArrow(b1,b2)) => (match (a2,b2) with …)` → CORRECT (0).
///   • SINGLE-sum nested match + self-recursion: `match a { TArrow(a1,a2) => match b { TArrow(b1,b2) =>
///     uni(a2,b2) } }` → CORRECT (0).
///   • ONLY the TUPLE-OF-TWO-SUMS match `match (a,b)` WITH a SELF-RECURSIVE call on the payload binders
///     fails. Both arg orders fail; recursing on the 1st components (a1,b1) fails the same way.
///
/// So: the self-call arg path for payload binders extracted by a TUPLE-of-sums (simultaneous 2-sum) match
/// passes stale/wrong values — the self-call omits something an ordinary `Core::Call` (separate helper)
/// gets. Same family as the still-live-binding self-call omitted-dup bugs (a self-recursive call reading a
/// payload binder that the tuple-match's shared scrutinee/payload aliases), now on the TUPLE-of-sums
/// simultaneous-match face. Fix locus likely backend/wasm/select.rs self-call arg emit for SumPayload
/// binders sourced from a tuple-pattern-over-two-sums desugar.
type Ty = TInt | TBool | TArrow(Ty, Ty)
def unify(a: Ty, b: Ty) = match (a, b) with
  | (Ty.TInt, Ty.TInt) => 1
  | (Ty.TBool, Ty.TBool) => 1
  | (Ty.TArrow(a1, a2), Ty.TArrow(b1, b2)) => unify(a2, b2)
  | (_, _) => 0
def run() = unify(Ty.TArrow(Ty.TInt, Ty.TBool), Ty.TArrow(Ty.TInt, Ty.TInt))
export { run }
